# Scratch queue rows EFB (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/EFB.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title SQ-EFB Earth fill on the placed blocks: water, air and earth replaced, 2026-11-02 ([structure_tuning.md](../structure_tuning.md) 3.8, 3.13, 3.28 to 3.30, 7.3.1, 7.5; TODO `structures/earthfill`, `structures/terrain #2`)
@@date 2026-11-02
@@jars creativeworldgen
@@sources feature_writeup/structure_tuning.md
@@text
@@text Targets patcherMod 1.1.07 **build/libs 2026-11-02 00:42** (not in `mods/` yet; prep_srv.sh swaps it in) with `waterReach` (new,
@@text default 2) and the `earth_fill/sand_base` tags, and the instance `[worldgen.earth_fill]`:
@@text `baseLayers` 3, `beardReach` 6 (air), `waterReach` 2 (water), `buryReach` 10, `maxMoundHeight` 8, `maxOverWater` 24, sizes small 24/8, medium 64/24,
@@text large 160/64, huge 320/128 (bounds 150/600/2000), `maxWaterSurplus` **0.5** (the instance value since 2026-11-02, was 0.0;
@@text the 7.5 writeup default; the code default is 0), `footprintMinWater` 9, `pruneMinWetColumns` 16, `beardFootprint` false, override `eugene:undead_castle=24,800,400`.
@@text Earth fill only cancels or prunes; the blocks are replaced by the vanilla beard (water and air under a bearded piece, out
@@text to `beardReach`; since 2026-11-02 earth over water deeper than `waterReach` 2 already counts toward `maxOverWater`, so deep fill is
@@text judged even where the beard could reach it) and by ground match (template earth swapped for the native ground). The earlier SQ-EF rows checked the
@@text log lines; these check that the world matches them. Probe: `/zq under <x> <z> <rChunks> [id text|-]` in
@@text `tools/scratch_query/zq_probe.js` (prep_srv.sh copies it in), **new 2026-11-02 and untested**: SQ-EFB-01 debugs it first.
@@text One group B fresh world, seed 8675309, scratch toml `[worldgen.earth_fill] log = "ALL"`. Chunky each square
@@text (`chunky center <x> <z>`, `chunky radius 300`, `chunky start`) and wait for it to finish before probing; a square is
@@text probed in tiles of `rChunks` 6 (the probe prints at most 30 starts per call). Every probe line is kept in
@@text `RES/rows/<ID>.log` for the comparison rows (11 to 13).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-EFB-00 | offline: worldgen tool tests (GroundMatch, EarthFill 113+, Meta print ALL)
@group none, offline
@commands `bash tools/test_worldgen_tools.sh`
@pass GroundMatchTest, EarthFillTest (113 or more checks) and MetaTest print `ALL` and no FAIL
@fails the failing test names the method; nothing to boot until it passes
@from batches/r1103w/w_1_B.qb passed
shell bash $INST/tools/test_worldgen_tools.sh > ../twt.txt 2>&1; grep -nE "^==|ALL|FAIL|error:|Could not find" ../twt.txt | head -60; ! grep -qE "FAIL|error:|Could not find or load main class" ../twt.txt

## SQ-EFB-01 | probe: /zq under at spawn prints full lines; earth-fill log has lines (log = ALL)
@group B
@commands boot; `grep -c '\[earth-fill\]' logs/latest.log`; spawn chunks loaded: `/zq under 0 0 4 -`
@pass probe prints `under ...` lines with all fields and a final `under: N starts`; no `Error occurred while handling event`; the earth-fill log has lines (log = ALL)
@fails Rhino errors: `getTagOrEmpty`, `getAllStarts`, `Heightmap$Types` names (memory `rhino-fieldandmethods-gotcha`); fix the probe in `tools/`, rerun
@from batches/r1103w/w_1r_B.qb
bootexpect \[earth-fill\]
> zq under {S1} {S3} 4 -
waitlog \[zq\] (under: \d+ starts|error) 120
expect \[zq\] under: \d+ starts
reject \[zq\] error
reject Error occurred while handling event
shell echo "earth-fill lines: $(grep -c "\[earth-fill\]" ../w1_all.log || true)"; grep "\[zq\] under " logs/latest.log | tail -5 | cut -c1-400
look the under lines carry every field (pieces, cols, air-below, water-below, base water, base earth, ring, foreign); 0 starts at an ocean spawn is a pass for the probe, rerun on a square tile (SQ-EFB-02) if so

## SQ-EFB-02 (air)
@group B
@commands inland plains / taiga square (`/locate biome minecraft:plains`, a spot with hills nearby), Chunky r 300; `/zq under` tiles over the square
@pass every kept start: `over6 0` (no column hangs more than `beardReach` over air); `air-below` columns only where the gap is 1 to 6 and the beard rounded them off; no village house standing on air
@fails `over6` > 0 on a kept start: find its `[earth-fill]` line; if it says `0 over air after beard` the count misses this piece kind (span, sunk piece, rotation), with the piece id
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-EFB-03 (air, mounds)
@group B
@commands hills square (`/locate biome minecraft:windswept_hills` or `terralith:highlands`), Chunky r 300; `grep 'mound columns'`
@pass every start whose line shows mound columns within its limit is kept and the probe shows `air-below 0` under it (the beard built the mound); every start over the mound limit is CANCELLED and has no probe line; LOOK at two mound starts from the side: an earth slope, no overhang, no stone pillar
@fails air under a kept mound start: the beard reach is shorter than the mound counted (`maxMoundHeight` 8 vs the size limit); note gap and size
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-EFB-04 (air, earthless pieces)
@group B
@commands same squares plus a desert and a jungle square; `/zq under` filtered `pyramid`, `igloo`, `jungle`, `camp`, `ruin` (`/zq under <x> <z> 6 camp`)
@pass legacy and earthless pieces (spans, 3.28): `over6 0` for kept ones; a camp or ruin with a column more than 6 over air has a CANCELLED line, not a world entry; tents and plinths sit on the ground (LOOK one camp, one ruin)
@fails floating camp kept: the span rule skipped it (`surface_structures` step or above sea level less `baseLayers`), note the structure id for `footprintAllPieces`
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-EFB-05 (water, lakes)
@group B
@commands check the scratch toml has `[worldgen.earth_fill] maxWaterSurplus = 0.5` (instance value since 2026-11-02); lake / river square (the SQ-EF-09 kind, `/locate biome minecraft:river` near plains), Chunky r 300; `grep -E 'too wet\|wet only\|footprint'`; `/zq under` tiles
@pass kept starts: `water-below` only with `max` 2 or less (`waterReach`; deeper water under earth counts, and over `maxOverWater` 24 the start goes), `base water 0` (no flooded floor) except `wet_ok` and pond structures; every `too wet` start has no probe line; no kept start has footprint water above 1.5 x its ground (60:40 passes, 61:39 goes) in its log line; record how many kept starts sit between 50:50 and 60:40 (kept at 0.5, cancelled at 0.0)
@fails water under a kept piece deeper than 2: `waterReach` not read (toml key missing, fallback) or the piece has no earth (add its base to `stone_base` / `sand_base`); base water in a house: the ground-level column was counted as ground (E12 lowest-layer rule); a kept start over 60:40: `maxWaterSurplus` not read (still 0.0 or the code default)
@draft no batch holds this row yet
